note as SAP_UNIVERSAL_JOURNAL_ALIGNMENT
  SAP-ALIGNED ACCOUNT ASSIGNMENT PRINCIPLE
  - The journal header identifies the accounting document; the ledger line is the posting unit.
  - journal_entry_assignments is a 1:1 extension of each ledger line and carries the
    controlling/subledger dimensions: business partner, asset, liability, contract,
    project/WBS, cost/profit center, internal order, source documents and payment.
  - A transaction can therefore affect many assets/liabilities and one asset/liability can
    participate in many transactions without forcing a false header-level relationship.
  - Exactly one active assignment row per ledger_entry_id; tenant consistency is enforced.
end note

